  "description": "It's BACK for 2025!! You wanted it, you got it. The Pro-X is coming back and now in more sizes - three 20\" and two 24\" sizes!! And we added a new color!! White!!\nIt's 1984. Mike Miranda is showboating around the world on it. Tommy Brackens is shredding tires off of his. It's the Torker PRO-X! You know you wanted one... Trust us, we did too, and that's part of why we brought it back for you.\nThe PRO-X was the first Torker to use the small triangle downtube gussets instead of the traditional sideplate gussets, and now this iconic frame is back as our FULLY MODERN RACE MACHINE with a 1 1/8\" threadless steertube, a 27.2 seatmast, V brakes, a Euro bottom bracket... you know all the modern BMX stuff that a modern BMX race bike should have. And of course it is full 4130 Cro-mo, as ALWAYS.\nModern Race Geometry:\nChrome Plated or White\nTraditional dual top tube race frame\nDouble Thick ( 1/4\" ) Laser Cut Cro-mo Dropouts\nModern Chainstay Brace\nIntegrated Campy® Headtube\n3/8\" dropouts front and rear",
